  "question": {
    "text": "For which of the following compounds Kjeldahl method can be used to determine the percentage of Nitrogen?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2SMFO",
      "text": "\nNitrobenzene\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ka8YP",
      "text": "\nPyridine\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QC4TT",
      "text": "\nAlanine\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "nsRev",
      "text": "\nDiazomethane",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Kjeldahl's method is not applicable for compounds containing nitrogen in nitro and azo groups and nitrogen present in the ring. Because nitrogen of these compounds does not change to ammonium sulphate under these conditions.\nHence only Alanine can be used to determine percentage of nitrogen.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/JBGRiWdRE0WGVVC14wnM_g_HzleGpIbd63K7f0s5iTc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
